    "status": "present",
    "value": "Minimize replacements by values within1..limit so every mirrored pair in the even-length array has the same sum. The approach is: difference-array sweep of each mirrored pair zero/one/two-replacement cost intervals. Its target cost is O(n+limit) time/O(limit) space. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
